  "mechanisms": [
    "The study primarily focuses on comparing satisfaction levels rather than proposing specific psychological mechanisms for the observed differences. It notes that differences, when present, are statistically significant but with negligible effect sizes, suggesting no strong underlying mechanism tied to LEED certification itself for occupant satisfaction."
  ],
  "moderators": [],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "LEED rating does not significantly affect building and workspace satisfaction, suggesting that LEED certification alone does not guarantee higher occupant satisfaction with IEQ.",
    "LEED certification does not significantly influence occupant satisfaction with indoor environmental quality parameters.",
    "Future LEED versions might benefit from attention to optimization of visual and thermal comfort, provision of added control, acoustic performance, and sound reduction.",
    "Development of post-occupancy evaluation protocols fully integrated into the accreditation system could improve LEED's impact on occupant satisfaction."
  ],
