  "limitations": [
    "The collection of user responses was not linked with direct appraisal and/or measurement of physical characteristics and IEQ parameters of the building and workspace.",
    "No systematic randomized approach was enforced for building selection, so the dataset is not a representative sample of the building stock.",
    "Other parameters not included in the CBE survey (e.g., availability of a view out, view layers, location) may have a significant influence on occupant satisfaction.",
    "The greatest majority of responses were obtained from buildings in the US (83%), limiting generalizability to other contexts.",
    "The sample of LEED buildings is only partially representative of the total amount of buildings rated by LEED to date, as the LEED program has continuously evolved.",
    "The study did not consider the potential influence of 'non-environmental' factors on occupant satisfaction in LEED and non-LEED certified buildings.",
    "Future studies are needed to investigate correlations between satisfaction, LEED certification level (e.g., Platinum, Gold), LEED product, and credit allocation within IEQ categories."
  ],
